{
  "id": "slack",
  "name": "Slack",
  "kind": "app",
  "category": "Communication",
  "match": {
    "windows_exe": [
      "slack.exe"
    ],
    "macos_bundle": [
      "com.tinyspeck.slackmacgap"
    ],
    "window_title": [
      "Slack"
    ]
  },
  "sources": [
    "https://slack.com/help/articles/201374536-Slack-keyboard-shortcuts"
  ],
  "note": "From the official 'Slack keyboard shortcuts' Help Center article, current as of 2026-09. Skipped as not expressible or not a fixed shortcut: mouse-only actions ('Expand or collapse all sidebar sections' and 'Mark a message as unread', both Option/Alt+Click); 'Switch to a specific workspace' and 'Switch to a specific tab', which use a generic Cmd/Ctrl+[number] pattern rather than one fixed chord; the clipboard-paste-as-hyperlink tip (Cmd/Ctrl+V), which is standard OS paste, not a distinct Slack shortcut. 'Add an emoji reaction to a message' lists 7 alternate punctuation keys (`, #, \\, _, ¡, à, 、) that are the same physical key on different keyboard layouts (marked * in the source); only the standard backtick variant is included. 'Jump to a conversation' (Ctrl+K / Ctrl+T) is documented for Windows/Linux only, with no Mac equivalent in this article, so mac is omitted for it. 'Open Help' (F1) and 'Underline selected text' (Cmd+U) are documented for Mac only; the article's Windows/Linux tables omit both. Shortcuts marked ** in the source (desktop-app only) are included without a note since this catalog entry only matches the desktop app. 'Resize the left sidebar' (Left/Right, needs the sidebar section focused via F6 first) is split into two directional actions.",
